Clarity v0.5 (retrieval only) against v0.12 (tools and a loop), 120 cases

                      v0.5    v0.12   change
  composite           83%     100%     +17%
  document            59%      97%     +38%
  unanswerable        95%      80%     -15%
  warehouse           20%      90%     +70%
  overall             60%      93%     +33%

  cases the newer system fixed : 46
  cases it broke               : 6
    tail-rotated-util, tail-termination, abstain-03, abstain-04, abstain-07, abstain-15

This is the comparison that survives contact with a manager, and the absolute
number is not it. Nobody can tell you whether 93% is good. Everybody can tell you
whether it beats what you had, by how much, and on which kinds of question.

Then read the second list. 46 cases got better and 6 got worse, and the
average contains both. Three of the regressions are refusals: the older system
said it did not know, and the newer one, holding a warehouse and four tools,
found something to say instead.

That is a real cost of Part IV, it is invisible in a single number, and it is
the kind of thing an eval set exists to catch.
